# Worker secrets only: copy to ignored .dev.vars and fill only the sources you use.
# Five built-in sources: GitHub, WakaTime, Codex, OpenRouter, Anthropic API.
# Active empty assignments let Deploy to Cloudflare discover optional secrets.
# Keep usernames, enable flags, periods and cache options in wrangler.jsonc vars.
# Explicit upload: npm run deploy -- --secrets-file .dev.vars
# Never put credentials in Wrangler vars, source control or README image URLs.

# GitHub username-only public REST needs no token. For full owner/private data:
# GitHub classic PAT/OAuth scopes: repo, read:user, read:org.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# WakaTime public-first needs no secret. Same-range OAuth fallback/token-only:
# Scopes: email plus read_stats.languages (or read_stats).
WAKATIME_TOKEN=

# Codex needs no secret input. After deployment, run npm run sync:codex locally;
# the helper creates, saves and installs its own private sync key automatically.

# OpenRouter Management key; an ordinary model-inference key is insufficient.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Reporting start OPENROUTER_USAGE_SINCE belongs in vars, not this upload file.

# Anthropic organization API usage, not Claude Pro/Max.
ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_USAGE_SINCE belongs in Wrangler vars if overriding its default.
